extraction_notes: |
  - Printed 60-62 (cache p061-p063), read from the text layer. The cache carries
    substituted digits on these pages (lD6, 1 1 8); dice were read as dice, and
    the attribute block was checked against a 200 dpi render of printed 61.
  - The Haven Mutant rules on printed 60 apply to all eight mutant R.C.C.s: G.M.
    approval, no O.C.C., no power armor or robots, no Juicer or M.O.M.
    conversion. They are in `restrictions`; no O.C.C. is stated as prose because
    the class grants its own secondary skills and so is not offered as needing
    one.
  - `xp_table` is the Haven Mutant ladder on printed 79 (the one for every
    mutant but the Shaman), stored as the lower bound of each band.
  - Secondary skills: the book rolls 1D4+3. `count` is a number, so the maximum
    (7) is stored and the roll is in the note. Decided at import; revisit if the
    picker is ever given a rolled count.
  - W.P. ancient versus modern is recorded in the choice-group notes, because
    the catalog does not split the Weapon Proficiencies category.
  - The +2 to disarm applies only to a Called Shot with a modern firearm or
    energy weapon, so it is a special ability rather than a bonus.
  - Horror Factor 12 applies when several Beast Men show up with big guns or
    odd devices; stored as text beside the base 9.
  - Starting money is the 1D6x100 credits. The 3D6x1000 in tradable goods is
    prose in GM Notes.
  - Starting gear not stored as rows: the Mutant Bone Axe and Bone Dagger (bone
    weapon rows arrive with the gear PR), one weapon per W.P., the watercolors
    and brushes, 1D6+2 cans of spray paint, 2D4 days of food and water, the web
    vest, the optional patchwork body armor of 4D6+6 M.D.C., a satchel and
    personal items. They are listed in GM Notes.
  - Shaman variant: its skills are added by the variant; the removal of Secondary, Piloting and modern W.P. skills, the prayers and the Shaman XP ladder are prose only; see BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT.md F108.
  - Shaman variant: the +3D6+10 P.P.E. is folded into the variant''s own
    `ppe_base` (2D6 + 3D6 = 5D6, plus 10) because the pool parser reads one dice
    term; the +1D6 per level is in the same formula. The +2 I.Q. and +1D4+2 M.A.
    are attribute bonuses on the variant, which restates the class''s other
    bonuses because a variant''s bonuses replace the class''s.
