## Lore

Beast Men are massive, upright mutants who look like a cross between a gorilla
and a Sasquatch: broad-chested, thick-armed, and covered in short fur that is
remarkably soft to the touch, with a tall crown of the same fur on the head.
Their faces are ape-like, and the men often wear long sideburns and a beard
braided into one to three tails. Their hands are fully human, just broad, and
their bones and hides are Mega-Damage tough.

For all the brutish looks, they are the thinkers of the mutant community. They
adore machines, and they also paint, write and do mathematics. They build the
armor, tune the vehicles and fix the weapons and radios the other clans rely
on, and they invented the motorized unicycles the Quill Men ride. Their work is
traded to the other mutants for food, salvage and favors. They are among the
very few mutants who can read, and they hunt for old technical manuals.

## GM Notes

Beast Men treat outsiders as invaders, and are usually the first to watch a
newcomer''s camp - more interested in the machines than the people. They will
slip in to study, tinker with or simply steal tools, generators, radios,
weapons, parts and even whole vehicles. Only their people''s distrust of magic
keeps them from being natural Techno-Wizards.

- **Alignment:** any; most are Scrupulous (25%), Unprincipled (20%) or
  Anarchist (40%).
- **Size:** 6-7 feet (1.8-2.1 m), 260-400 lbs (117-180 kg).
- **Life span:** about 80 years, a few reaching 118; females live 2D4 years
  longer.
- **Average NPC level:** 1D6+5. Player characters start at level one.
- **Attacks:** by Hand to Hand: Expert, four at level one.
- **Money:** 1D6x100 credits, plus 3D6x1000 in tradable goods - tech, parts,
  pre-Rifts curios, or loot from outsiders.
- **Other gear:** a Mutant Bone Axe and a bone dagger, one weapon for each
  W.P., watercolors and brushes, 1D6+2 cans of spray paint in different colors,
  2D4 days of food and water, a web vest with pockets for tools and parts, a
  satchel, personal items, and patchwork body armor of 4D6+6 M.D.C. that most
  never bother to wear.
- **Habitat:** at or below street level, in clean lairs full of comforts.
  Their territory is easy to spot from its murals and artistic graffiti.
- **Allies and enemies:** friendly enough with other mutants, wary of the
  Knights of the White Rose (not mutants, users of magic, and liable to go mad
  in the ruins), and trading partners but not friends of the Horune Pirates and
  Splugorth slavers. Their foes are outsiders, ghosts, monsters,
  Undead Horrors, madmen and creatures of magic.

## Mutant Shaman

Every sizable clan is led by a Shaman, who keeps the race''s own attributes and
powers and gains the following. Choose the **Beast Man Shaman** variant.

- **Attributes and P.P.E.:** +2 I.Q., +1D4+2 M.A., +3D6+10 starting P.P.E. and
  +1D6 P.P.E. per level. The variant carries these.
- **Shaman skills:** Animal Husbandry (+10%), Literacy in the native language
  (American, +15%), Brewing: Medicinal (+15%), Dance (+10%), Fasting (+20%),
  History: Pre-Rifts (+10%), Holistic Medicine (+10%), History:
  Post-Apocalypse (+20%), Sing (+10%), Public Speaking (+20%) and Veterinary Science (+10%). The
  variant adds these.
- **What they replace:** these skills take the place of ALL Secondary Skills,
  all Piloting skills and all modern W.P.s. A Shaman never uses a modern weapon,
  vehicle or machine. The app cannot remove skills through a variant, so a
  Shaman player should leave the secondary, pilot and modern W.P. picks empty.
- **Role:** Shamans make the clan''s laws, judge its disputes and lead the clan
  and tribe.
- **Prayers to Isis, the Mighty Lady.** Prayer of Strength: 01-20%, +5% per
  level, to be heard; if it is, +6 P.S., +1D4x10 M.D.C., and 48 hours without
  food or water with no ill effect. Usable up to six times a year. Prayer of
  Inspiration or Wisdom: 01-12%, +3% per level (+10% after a week of fasting);
  if heard, a dream vision brings insight, an idea or a caution concerning
  whatever was prayed about.
- **Experience:** a Shaman advances on the "Gateway Knight & Mutant Shaman"
  ladder (printed 79), not the Haven Mutant one: 0, 2,351, 4,701, 9,401,
  18,801, 28,001, 38,001, 53,001, 77,001, 102,001, 143,001, 195,201, 240,401,
  310,601, 360,801.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'beast-men');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'beast-men';

